// expect: 6
// The rest of a generic record pattern is whatever the caller's record has
// beyond the named field, so it can only be built under the twin that knows
// the record. The residual was computed once, at lower, from the generic
// receiver; its row was open, so the build floored with no diagnostic.
// Measured on boot 0bc8383e: exit 134 at `record rest on unresolved
// receiver`, zero diagnostics.
fn drop_a(r) = {
  let {a, ...rest} = r
  rest
}

fn main() = drop_a({a: 1, b: 2}).b + drop_a({a: 1, b: 3, c: 4}).c
